      <Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART IV, SECTION D AND SECTION E:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>HOLDCO WAS FORMED ON JANUARY 19, 2024, TO SERVE AS THE PARENT ENTITY FOR COUNCIL OF COMMUNITY CLINICS AND COMMUNITY CLINICS HEALTH NETWORK, IN CONNECTION WITH A SYSTEM-WIDE REORGANIZATION. SUCH SYSTEM-WIDE REORGANIZATION NEEDED APPROVAL BY THE CALIFORNIA ATTORNEY GENERAL PRIOR TO IMPLEMENTATION, AND THE CALIFORNIA ATTORNEY GENERAL WAS UNWILLING TO REVIEW THE REORGANIZATION UNTIL THE INTERNAL REVENUE SERVICE GRANTED HOLDCO'S TAX-EXEMPT STATUS. HOLDCO RECEIVED ITS DETERMINATION LETTER IN OCTOBER 2024. THEREFORE, AS OF THE END OF HOLDCO'S FIRST FISCAL YEAR ON JUNE 30, 2024, THE CALIFORNIA ATTORNEY GENERAL HAD NOT YET APPROVED THE SYSTEM-WIDE REORGANIZATION, AND HOLDCO REMAINED INACTIVE. THE CALIFORNIA ATTORNEY GENERAL'S APPROVAL WAS RECEIVED DECEMBER 31, 2024, SO NOW HOLDCO AND ITS SUPPORTED ORGANIZATIONS, COUNCIL OF COMMUNITY CLINICS AND COMMUNITY CLINICS HEALTH NETWORK, WILL IMPLEMENT THE REORGANIZATION, THEREBY CAUSING HOLDCO TO BECOME THE PARENT OF BOTH SUPPORTED ORGANIZATIONS, WITH THE POWER TO APPOINT THE SUPPORTED ORGANIZATIONS' DIRECTORS AND EXERCISE A SUBSTANTIAL DEGREE OF DIRECTION OF THE SUPPORTED ORGANIZATIONS' POLICIES, PROGRAMS AND ACTIVITIES.</ExplanationTxt>
      </Form990ScheduleAPartVIGrp>
